# Copy to .env and fill in the two values below to broadcast. Everything else already has a working default.

# Account and permission doing the proposing, required to broadcast. A permission scoped to eosio.msig with linkauth covers it; CONTRIBUTING.md describes the setup. The proposer pays the RAM for the proposal row and gets it back when the proposal executes or is cancelled.
PROPOSER_PERMISSION=youraccount@active
# Key satisfying that permission, in PVT_K1_ form, required to broadcast.
PROPOSER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# API node the tooling reads and broadcasts through. Defaults to the value shown.
#NODEOS_API_URL=https://vaulta.greymass.com

# Any flag a builder declares may also be set here, as VP_ plus its name uppercased with dashes as underscores: --commit becomes VP_COMMIT, --build-dir becomes VP_BUILD_DIR. A flag passed on the command line wins over this file, and propose prints the source of every value it resolves. `bun run propose <vp> <name> --help` lists the flags a builder declares. A value that changes per broadcast, such as the cited commit, usually belongs on the command line rather than here.
